{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546535927,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb172a1ffej1jOZ3ysNoYkNr","part":{"partID":"prt_1d34f0a44002y7rFJrrlCEhZlp","sessionID":"ses_e2cb172a1ffej1jOZ3ysNoYkNr","messageID":"msg_1d34efe1e001JRjYp8XOga48zO","type":"tool","id":"call_413a065fa88147e494d47a8e","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/plugins/README.md","oldString":"and suppresses a repeated transform for the same message and exposes `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status`. |","newString":"and suppresses a repeated transform for the same message and exposes `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status`. Its recommendation mapper keeps each CLI row's `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` and `needsMode` under the names `renderAdvisorBrief` reads, so an OpenCode brief names the same command and policy as a hook brief. |"},"output":"Edited .opencode/plugins/README.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".opencode/plugins/README.md","patch":"Index: .opencode/plugins/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- .opencode/plugins/README.md\n+++ .opencode/plugins/README.md\n@@ -153,9 +153,9 @@\n \n | File | Responsibility |\n |---|---|\n | `opencode-goal.js` | The largest plugin. Owns the goal state machine, supervisor, continuation, capabilities and the goal tool surface. Hooks session, message, permission and question events, `experimental.chat.system.transform` and a family of goal tools. |\n-| `system-skill-advisor.js` | Spawns the skill-advisor subprocess on a prompt-cache miss, manages a TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, integrates transform-dedup where the opt-in same-message dedup bases its decision on the full advisor block before directive-lifecycle reduction and suppresses a repeated transform for the same message and exposes `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status`. |\n+| `system-skill-advisor.js` | Spawns the skill-advisor subprocess on a prompt-cache miss, manages a TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, integrates transform-dedup where the opt-in same-message dedup bases its decision on the full advisor block before directive-lifecycle reduction and suppresses a repeated transform for the same message and exposes `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status`. Its recommendation mapper keeps each CLI row's `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` and `needsMode` under the names `renderAdvisorBrief` reads, so an OpenCode brief names the same command and policy as a hook brief. |\n | `system-spec-gate.js` | Maps OpenCode's transport onto the runtime-neutral spec-gate core. Classify best-effort fetches the last user message via `ctx.client`. Enforce throws `system-spec-gate:` on deny. `event` sweeps, advances and evicts state. |\n | `sk-code-post-edit-quality.js` | Correlates `tool.execute.before` file paths to `tool.execute.after` callIDs, runs the post-edit router core and drains findings on the next transform. |\n | `lib/v2-bridge.js` | Builds the dual export for every bridged plugin. `server` is the unchanged v1 factory, and `setup` maps its hooks onto OpenCode 2 registrations and returns a cleanup function. |\n | `lib/tool-identity.js` | The `tool` identity helper. Returns a v1 tool definition unchanged and carries zod as `tool.schema`. |\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .opencode/plugins/README.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/plugins/README.md\",\"oldString\":\"and suppresses a repeated transform for the same message and exposes `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status`. |\",\"newString\":\"and suppresses a repeated transform for the same message and exposes `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status`. Its recommendation mapper keeps each CLI row's `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` and `needsMode` under the names `renderAdvisorBrief` reads, so an OpenCode brief names the same command and policy as a hook brief. |\"}"},"time":{"start":1794546534980,"end":1794546535927}}}}
