{"type":"text","timestamp":1794546552751,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb172a1ffej1jOZ3ysNoYkNr","part":{"id":"prt_1d34f4f29002GDmO0A5gQp61PL","sessionID":"ses_e2cb172a1ffej1jOZ3ysNoYkNr","messageID":"msg_1d34f42a40012uRj56F7fFk1oj","type":"text","text":"T040 done.\n\n**File written:** `.opencode/plugins/README.md` (one line, section 6 `KEY FILES`, the `system-skill-advisor.js` row).\n\nThe row now reads that its recommendation mapper keeps each CLI row's `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` and `needsMode` under the names `renderAdvisorBrief` reads, so an OpenCode brief names the same command and policy as a hook brief. The diff is exactly 1 insertion and 1 deletion, no other line touched.\n\n**Verify output** (run from the repository root):\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"ownerSkillId\" .opencode/plugins/README.md\n1\n$ rg -c \"renderAdvisorBrief\" .opencode/plugins/README.md\n1\n```\n\nBoth match the expected counts. Nothing was left undone, no checkbox was ticked and no other file was modified.","time":{"start":1794546552617,"end":1794546552751}}}
